WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:02.180
Welcome to Use ref exercise one.

1
00:00:02.519 --> 00:00:03.250
In this exercise,

2
00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:06.010
we'll create a ref to access a text input element

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.380
and implement a button that when clicked,

4
00:00:08.609 --> 00:00:09.989
focuses the input field.

5
00:00:10.329 --> 00:00:11.270
Let's solve it.

6
00:00:11.689 --> 00:00:11.930
First,

7
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.329
we import react and use ref from React.

8
00:00:18.659 --> 00:00:19.180
Second,

9
00:00:19.579 --> 00:00:21.979
let's declare a reference using Uref

10
00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:22.739
type.

11
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.139
Constant input ref equals use ref with null.

12
00:00:26.889 --> 00:00:28.829
Now let's handle the focus functionality.

13
00:00:29.409 --> 00:00:31.690
Create a function called handle focus.

14
00:00:32.539 --> 00:00:33.458
Inside the function,

15
00:00:33.539 --> 00:00:33.999
type

16
00:00:34.298 --> 00:00:37.098
input rev.current.focus.

17
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:38.310
Next,

18
00:00:38.439 --> 00:00:39.479
in the return statement,

19
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.939
declare an input field.

20
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.139
Set its ref attribute to input ref and it's type to text.

21
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:49.819
Finally,

22
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.099
implement a button.

23
00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.700
Set the buttons on click attribute to call handle focus.

24
00:00:55.419 --> 00:00:56.450
Inside the button,

25
00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:57.759
write the text,

26
00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.360
focus the input.

27
00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:01.430
Let's see it in action.

28
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.239
When we click the button labeled focus the input,

29
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.279
the input field gains focus.

30
00:01:08.389 --> 00:01:09.589
See you in the next lesson.